  "database": "rschema_0165",
  "nl_text": "The database schema named \"rschema_0165\" contains four tables: Meteorological_Station, Operator, Historical_Evolution_Information, and Audit_Information.\nThe Meteorological_Station table represents a meteorological station, with columns for Elevation (FLOAT), Geographic_Environment_Description (VARCHAR(255)), Latitude (FLOAT), Longitude (FLOAT), Observation_Elements_List (VARCHAR(255)), Observation_Instrument_Name_and_Model (VARCHAR(255)), Observation_Record_Medium (VARCHAR(255)), Observation_Standards (VARCHAR(255)), Observation_Time (DATETIME), Station_ID (INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY), and Station_Name and Station_Type (VARCHAR(255)).\nThe Operator table holds information about the operators, with columns for Email (VARCHAR(255)), Level (VARCHAR(255)), Name (VARCHAR(255)), Operator_ID (INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY), Phone (INTEGER), and Role (VARCHAR(255)).\nThe Historical_Evolution_Information table contains information about changes made to the meteorological station, with columns for Belonging_Station_ID (INTEGER, NOT NULL), Change_ID (INTEGER, PRIMARY KEY), Change_Type (VARCHAR(255)), End_Time (DATETIME), New_Value (VARCHAR(255)), Old_Value (VARCHAR(255)), Operation_Status (VARCHAR(255)), Operation_Time (DATETIME), Operator_ID (INTEGER), Reason_for_Change (VARCHAR(255)), Start_Time (DATETIME), and Station_ID (INTEGER). The Belonging_Station_ID is a foreign key referencing the Station_ID in the Meteorological_Station table.\nFinally, the Audit_Information table records the audit information, with columns for Audit_Comments (VARCHAR(255)), Audit_Status (VARCHAR(255)), Audit_Time (DATETIME), Change_ID (INTEGER, NOT NULL), Operator_ID (INTEGER, NOT NULL), and is the PRIMARY KEY for these three columns. The Change_ID and Operator_ID are foreign keys referencing the Change_ID and Operator_ID in the Historical_Evolution_Information table, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "The meteorological information management system is designed to record and manage meteorological station information, historical evolution information, operator information, and audit records. Meteorological station information includes Station ID, Station Type (such as national station, regional station, marine station, sounding station, etc.), Station Name, Latitude, Longitude, Elevation, Geographic Environment Description, Observation Elements List, Observation Instrument Name and Model, Observation Time, Observation Record Medium, Observation Standards, and other relevant information. Historical evolution information includes Change ID, Station ID, Change Type (such as station name, station number, station location, observation elements, observation instruments, observation time, observation record medium, observation standards, etc.), Old Value, New Value, Start Time, End Time, Reason for Change, Operator ID, Operation Time, and Operation Status (such as pending selection, selected, historical data, etc.). Operator information includes Operator ID, Operator Name, Operator Level (such as provincial, city, county), Operator Role (such as system administrator, city and county user, etc.), Operator Email, and Operator Phone. Audit records include Change ID, Operator ID, Audit Time, Audit Status (such as approved, not approved), and Audit Comments. The system shall support operators in making changes to meteorological station information, recording historical evolutions, submitting audit requests, and auditors in reviewing change records and recording audit results. Each meteorological station can have multiple historical evolution records, each of which requires auditing, and each operator can submit multiple change records and participate in audits. The system shall be able to generate station change reports based on historical evolution information and record audit status and operators' operation history.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0165.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0165\nCREATE TABLE `meteorological_station` (\n  `station_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `station_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `station_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `elevation` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `geographic_environment_description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `latitude` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `longitude` float DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_elements_list` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_instrument_name_and_model` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_record_medium` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_standards` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`station_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `operator` (\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `level` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`operator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `historical_evolution_information` (\n  `change_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `belonging_station_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `change_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `old_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `new_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operator_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reason_for_change` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`change_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `historical_evolution_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`belonging_station_id`) REFERENCES `meteorological_station` (`station_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `historical_evolution_information_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`operator_id`) REFERENCES `operator` (`operator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `audit_information` (\n  `change_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `audit_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `audit_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `audit_comments` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`change_id`, `operator_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `audit_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`change_id`) REFERENCES `historical_evolution_information` (`change_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `audit_information_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`operator_id`) REFERENCES `operator` (`operator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
